From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:44:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 58/61] hottyterm: surfaces follow the system's reduced-motion
 setting

Watch GtkSettings gtk-enable-animations and NSWorkspace accessibility display changes. Keep the preference before the lazy hotty-blitz host exists, pass it through hotty_host_set_reduced_motion, and repaint idle surfaces on a change. Disconnect the platform observers before their surface is freed.

Adds 17 lines to upstream files: two GTK lifecycle hooks, the namespaced embedded bridge and header, and AppKit preference hooks. Host logic stays in src/termio/hotty.zig.

Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1-sol (Codex) <noreply@openai.com>
